From 4625f59feb8588518df66b1187246b0072e3539b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1E Refactor <dev@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:05:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Walking-distance geography + one-screen CN quick assign

Geography
- Replace hall-membership scoring with a corridor graph built from the real
  floor-plan coordinates and searched with Dijkstra. 122+114 previously scored
  'very good cluster' because both are Hall C, despite being opposite ends of
  the west wing.
- Delete every hard-coded room-number rule (UNSAFE_ICU_PAIRS,
  PREFERRED_ICU_PAIRS, the 103 / 122-114 helpers, the 103/104/113/114 quartet
  repair). All are now derived from distance bands.
- Fix a contradiction: the engine actively preferred pairing 122 ICU with 113,
  which is the longest walk on the unit.
- ROOM_POSITIONS moves into config/geography.ts so the map and the engine can
  no longer disagree. Derived adjacency replaces the hand-listed version, which
  claimed 113 was adjacent to 122.
- New tightenGeography pass swaps rooms between nurses when it lowers the worst
  walk without breaking ratio, capability, or CN intent.

Charge Nurse workflow
- Rapid acuity and flag coding now render on Current Staffing. Previously
  quickMode hid RapidRoomTools and the room detail panel entirely, so acuity
  and flags were unreachable on the CN's primary screen.
- One board component for both Current Staffing and Next Shift Plan.
- Auto / Fill Unassigned / Print / Excel promoted out of the collapsed
  'More tools' section into the always-visible action bar.
- Room detail becomes a floating exception panel instead of a third column.
- Add Expected Admission flag (vacant-room demand, does not raise census).

Semi-Auto locking
- Separate fixed rooms from locked nurses. Pre-assigning one room previously
  capped that nurse for the rest of the run; the CN normally seeds a nurse's
  sickest patient and still expects Semi-Auto to fill to ratio.
- Add a per-nurse lock toggle on the nurse rail.

Repo hygiene
- Add .gitignore; node_modules and dist were previously uncovered.
